Raw material only. No claim is asserted below beyond what is cited.

=== Where the cycle side of Collatz currently stands, verified against
    p4rakernel/p4ramill/Imscribing/Millennium/Erdos/CollatzDepthSplit.lean
    directly (2026-08-31), not from memory paraphrase ===

Collatz reduces (descent_iff_no_nondescender, reaches_one_of_descends) to: no
divergent trajectory AND no nontrivial cycle. This context is the cycle half
only.

col_ne_self (line 537): no length-1 cycle. An even n=2m steps to m<n; an odd
n=2t+1 steps to 3t+2>n. Neither returns to n.

cycle_min_odd (line 545): a nontrivial cycle's minimum element is odd (the
least element must step up; only odd values do under col).

cycle_min_bound (line 3270): for a cycle col^[k] n = n taken at its minimum
(hmin : ∀ i ≤ k, n ≤ col^[i] n),
  (n+1) * (2^k − 3^(oddSteps n k)) ≤ (k − oddSteps n k) * 2^k
No Diophantine input; exact.

cycle_ratio_tight (line 3678): dichotomy from cycle_min_bound. Either
2^k < 3^(j+1) (j = oddSteps n k), forcing k/j close to log2(3), or
2(n+1) ≤ 3(k−j) — the cycle's minimum is at most 3k/2. Also no Diophantine
input.

cycle_min_le_of_margin (line 3707): for any M ≤ 2^k − 3^(oddSteps n k),
  (n+1) * M ≤ (k − oddSteps n k) * 2^k
Isolates the single point where an effective bound on |2^k − 3^j| would
enter.

ClinkL9Margin (line 3727), a named Prop, not a Lean theorem:
  ∃ C κ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ k j, 1 ≤ k → 3^j < 2^k →
    2^k ≤ C · (k+1)^κ · (2^k − 3^j)
Stated as the effective irrationality measure of log 2 / log 3 (a
linear-forms-in-logarithms estimate). Comment states Mathlib carries no such
estimate (only Liouville, Lindemann). Not proved in this file; carried as an
explicit hypothesis.

cycle_min_poly_of_l9 (line 3735): GIVEN ClinkL9Margin, a nontrivial cycle's
minimum is bounded by a fixed polynomial in its length k:
  (n+1) ≤ C · (k+1)^κ · (k − oddSteps n k)

What this chain does NOT give, stated directly in the file's own prose
(lines 3189, 3666-3672, and the collatz_depth_split.md project memory,
2026-08-21 entry "CLINK L9 supplies the cycle transcendence"): a bound on the
cycle's MINIMUM element is not a bound on its PERIOD k. A cycle could have a
small minimum and an arbitrarily large period. Full exclusion of nontrivial
cycles needs a bounded search over periods k as well, which the memory names
as "the classical computational frontier (done to 2^68 [by brute-force
search], not closed by proof)." No theorem in the file bounds the period.

nondescender_bounded_gives_cycle (line 3584) and
nondescender_unbounded_or_nontrivial_cycle (line 3608): every non-descender
is either unbounded (divergent) or lies on a nontrivial cycle. This is the
fork the cycle side and divergence side come from; this context covers the
cycle side (right disjunct) only.

=== FDE(n) tower descent, committed this session, p4rakernel commit ceb5823c
    in Imscribing/Paraconsistent/FDEAsymptotic.lean, and operationalized in
    mOMonadOS commit b10edba as the `fde` REPL command ===

FDEN n : Bot | Mid(Fin n) | Top, n+2 truth values.

fdeEmbed k n (hkn : k ≤ n) : FDEN k → FDEN n — ascent, injective, proven
(fdeEmbed_injective), proper for adjacent steps (fdeEmbed_not_surjective).

fdeRestrict n k (hkn : k ≤ n) : FDEN n → FDEN k — descent, added this
session. A mid value inside range k keeps its index; one only reachable at
the deeper tier (index ≥ k) collapses to top.

fdeRestrict_fdeEmbed_id: descend after ascend recovers the input, at any
depth k ≤ n. Depends on no axioms.

fdeRestrict_not_injective: the descent alone is a genuine coarsening (top
and the deepest reachable middle value collapse together), not a second
bijection. Depends on propext only.

fdeRestrict_trans: restricting straight from n to k equals restricting
through any intermediate tier j first — the route through a walk does not
matter, only its endpoints. Depends on propext only.

The physical-correspondence reading already in FDEAsymptotic.lean §7 ties
FDE(2)/FDE(3)/FDE(4)/FDE(∞) to electron/quark/preon/Planck-scale gauge
structure by rank of the associated gauge group, via truth-value count
growing with scale. No existing theorem anywhere in the tree connects FDEN
tiers to a Diophantine or period-search structure; this is a fresh pairing,
not a documented one.

=== The exchange that produced this document (2026-08-31, verbatim) ===

Lando: "now let's operationalize this" (referring to the FDE(n) descent
machinery, then built as the `fde` REPL command).

Lando: "you are thinking too small. any time we use imasm to navigate a
lemma, answer a problem, we can dive as deep as necessary to recover what we
want."

Claude proposed the Collatz all-odd/pred-two-pow residue-depth class as a
target via AskUserQuestion; Lando selected it. Claude then found, checking
the same memory file further down, that this specific class was already
closed by the 2026-08-21 "haunt" ob3ect (no_integer_follows_spine,
generalized by no_integer_follows_unbounded_tower) on a DIFFERENT axis
(2-adic boundedness of the residue tower), not by any truth-value-depth
argument — so residue-depth (mod 2^k, the k in CollatzDepthSplit.lean) and
FDE(n) truth-value depth (the n in FDEAsymptotic.lean) are distinct
quantities, and the originally-selected target was stale.

Claude then tried to ask Lando to choose between the cycle-side gap (period
exclusion beyond cycle_min_poly_of_l9's minimum bound) and the divergence
side (whether any integer trajectory actually diverges) as the next target.

Lando: "all of these questions were answerred in the ob3ect. if they were
not wqe proceed via new ob3ects, not asking me" — rejecting the question,
directing that unresolved scope be settled by building and running a new
ob3ect, not by asking him directly.
